name bfm-pointblank-1
timeout 300

# THE ROLL-RATE LIMITER'S OWN INSTRUMENT — a synthetic swinging stimulus, built out of geometry.
#
# WHAT IT STIMULATES. The BFM law rolls the lift vector onto a bearing, and a bearing law is a bad
# signal at short range: the line of sight sweeps at V/R, so at 0.8 nm and 800 kt of combined closure it
# crosses the whole hemisphere in a couple of seconds. The commanded roll therefore does not merely
# saturate, it SWINGS IN AMPLITUDE AND SIGN, tick after tick. That is exactly the input under which a
# roll limiter built as a recursion on its OWN PREVIOUS COMMAND has no fixed point (doc/pilot.md 5.7) —
# so this file is not a fight, it is a stimulus. bfm-merge.fbm is the same head-on entry at 3 nm, where
# the sweep is an order of magnitude slower and the limiter is never asked the hard question.
#
# WHY 0.8 nm AND NOT CLOSER. Below ~0.6 nm the pursuer's ACM box never builds a track at all (measured:
# zero contacts for the whole run at 0.3 nm, and the pilot flies the cold search), so there is no
# bearing to swing and nothing is stimulated. 0.8 nm is the closest entry that still holds a lock for
# the whole run — 252 s of it — which is what makes the roll trace continuous enough to read.
#
# WHAT IS READ OFF IT. The achieved roll rate against the cap the code declares, from rollDeg
# differentiated at the 10 Hz sample rate, plus whether core/FBFlightMonitor calls a departure:
#
#   MEASURED, recursion limiter (|cmd_prev|*cap/|p|, its cap 60 deg/s): peak 82.0 deg/s = 1.37x its own
#   cap, 9.2 s spent above it.
#   MEASURED, plant-inversion limiter (its cap 90 deg/s):               peak 80.5 deg/s = 0.89x its own
#   cap, 0.0 s above it.
#
# The two peaks are within 2 %: the jet rolls the same. What changed is that the number in the source is
# now the bound — the old one was a nominal its own loop rang straight through.
#
# NEITHER RUN DEPARTS. The departure this stimulus is built around was seen in an intermediate build;
# the committed law does not produce one here, and that is the claim this file carries.
#
# IT ENDS IN TIMEOUT (exit 3), like every fight (bfm-basic.fbm's header). The verdict is the roll trace.

unit viper
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.67485 6.919403 4000 270.0 380     # 0.8 nm dead ahead of bandit, pointing straight at him
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode acm_hud
  set task bfm

unit bandit
  module f16
  team hostile
  spawn 46.67485 6.90000 4000 90.0 300       # the same defender as bfm-merge: a steady break turn
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  wp 46.70000 6.90000 4000 300               # the CENTRE of its turn — see bfm-basic.fbm's header
